# Scroll Substrate

Decisions: `docs/overhaul/EXPERIENCE_DECISIONS.md` (`X#`), `docs/overhaul/PLATFORM_DECISIONS.md` (`P#`). The as-built delta at the end of each, and `docs/CURRENT.md`, records open differences (snap type, client-rendered landing, deck `deltaX`, scheduler off at boot). Do not close those in a feature PR. Otherwise the contracts win on conflict; fix this rule in the same PR.

## Locked base

Do not edit `core/`, `substrate/`, `lib/orchestratorFsm.ts`, or `app/layout.tsx` to ship a feature. Features live in `features/<id>/`, import Jarvis only via `@/sdk`, register with one line in `features/index.ts`.

`JarvisRoot` owns the only WebGL context for the tab (one canvas → worker OffscreenCanvas). Never open a second `getContext("webgl"|"webgl2")` on `/`. Lenis + the scroll director own page scroll — features never add scroll/wheel listeners or call `window.scrollTo` / `scrollIntoView`.

## Layers

Use Tailwind z-tokens only — never a raw `z-index`: `z-backdrop` L0 · `z-substrate` L1 · `z-content` L2 · `z-decor` / `z-chrome` L3 · `z-modal` · `z-toast` · `z-landing`.

## SDK today

`defineFeature`, `defineCard`, `Slot`, `useSection`, `useTopic`, `useDraft`, `useTaskQueue`, `useWeatherLine`, `useJarvisState`, `useJarvisSend`, `useSpeak`, `useOrb`, `requestApproval`, `useFeatureQuery`, `useFeatureMutation`, `useActiveSession`, `useFeatureFlag`, `useToast`, `useReducedMotion`, `api`.

```ts
defineFeature({
  id: "toolwear",
  title: "Tool wear",
  cards: [{
    id: "toolwear.recent", slot: "monitor.rail", order: 40, size: "md",
    component: lazy(() => import("./RecentInsertsCard")),
  }],
});
```

Place cards with `<Slot id="monitor.rail" />`. Use `useTopic` for SSE; `useDraft` for local baton text.

## Hard don'ts

- Second WebGL context, feature `requestAnimationFrame` loops, or feature scroll/wheel listeners
- Raw `z-index` or `position: fixed` outside L3 chrome
- Inventing prices, rates, or dimensions with no tool/master-data source
- External/destructive acts without HITL Authorize (mail, calendar write, quote send, sheet write)
- Treating a parked approval as authorized
